  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nYou can do the following operation on the array **atmost once**:\n\n\nChoose any **non-negative** integer XXX and a subarray [L,R][L, R][L,R] (1≤L≤R≤N)(1 \\leq L \\leq R \\leq N)(1≤L≤R≤N) and update Ai=Ai&amp;XA_i = A_i \\&amp; XAi​=Ai​&amp;X for all L≤i≤RL \\leq i \\leq RL≤i≤R. Here &amp;\\&amp;&amp; denotes bitwise AND operation.\nFind the **maximum** bitwise XOR of **all** the elements of the updated array you can achieve.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nFirst line of each test case contains an integer NNN - denoting the length of array AAA.\nSecond line contains NNN integers A1,A2,…ANA_1, A_2, \\dots A_NA1​,A2​,…AN​ - denoting the array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the **maximum** XOR of all the elements of the updated array you can achieve.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2300 \\leq A_i \\lt 2^{30}0≤Ai​&lt;230",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases do not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n3 3 3 3\n3\n1 6 4",
        "output": "3\n7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: We can choose the subarray [L,R][L,R][L,R] as [2,4][2,4][2,4] and X=0X=0X=0. Thus, A2=3&0=0,A3=3&0=0,A_2 = 3\\&0 = 0, A_3 = 3\\&0 = 0,A2​=3&0=0,A3​=3&0=0, and A4=3&0=0A_4 = 3\\&0 = 0A4​=3&0=0. The updated array is [3,0,0,0][3,0,0,0][3,0,0,0]. The bitwise XOR of all the elements of the updated array is 3⊕0⊕0⊕0=33\\oplus 0\\oplus 0\\oplus 0 = 33⊕0⊕0⊕0=3.\nIt can be shown that the bitwise XOR of the updated array cannot exceed 333 after applying at most one operation.\nTest Case 222: We can choose the subarray [L,R][L,R][L,R] as [1,2][1,2][1,2] and X=3X=3X=3. Thus, A1=1&3=1A_1 = 1\\&3 = 1A1​=1&3=1 and A2=6&3=2A_2 = 6\\&3 = 2A2​=6&3=2. The updated array is [1,2,4][1, 2, 4][1,2,4]. The bitwise XOR of all the elements of the updated array is 1⊕2⊕4=71\\oplus 2\\oplus 4 = 71⊕2⊕4=7.\nIt can be shown that the bitwise XOR of the updated array cannot exceed 777 after applying at most one operation."
      }
    ]
  },
